<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<!--
  All user-facing Chinese text lives here rather than inline in the composables.

  Not ceremony: string resources are what the system uses for font-scale and
  locale handling, and inline literals are the reason apps ship with text that
  clips at 1.3x font scale. It also makes the copy reviewable in one place, which
  matters because the wording here is doing real work — most of it is telling
  someone what to do about a failure.
-->
